## 4. The Async Loop Hang

**What happened:** After setting up the `Apply to each` loop with `Execute Agent and wait` steps, the loop completed all iterations (showing green checkmarks on each) but did not close. The flow hung for 20+ minutes without progressing to the next step.

**Root cause:** The `Execute Agent and wait` connector uses an asynchronous webhook pattern (`OpenApiConnectionWebhook`). Power Automate waits for all async callbacks from all iterations to fully resolve before releasing the loop. When iterations run in parallel (the default), callback resolution can stall indefinitely.

**The fix:** Set `Apply to each` concurrency to 1 in the Settings tab. This forces sequential execution — one iteration fully completes (including webhook closure) before the next begins. The loop is slower but reliable.

