## 5. Word Template Must Use Content Controls, Not Text Placeholders

**What happened:** The first version of the Word template used `{{REPORT_DATE}}` style text tokens. The Power Automate `Populate a Word template` step returned: "The selected file doesn't contain template elements" and failed with a `BadRequest`.

**Root cause:** The `Populate a Word template` action in Power Automate's Word Online (Business) connector exclusively recognizes native Word Content Controls — form fields inserted via the Developer tab. Text placeholders in any format are not recognized.

**The fix:** Open the template in Word desktop, enable the Developer tab, and insert Plain Text Content Controls at each placeholder location. Name each control in Properties to match the variable names used in the flow.

