## 6. DLP Policies Can Block Agent-Flow Combinations

**What happened:** An early version of the agent was blocked by a Data Loss Prevention (DLP) policy conflict. The Copilot Studio knowledge source connector was classified as "Non-business" while the Word Online and SharePoint connectors used in the flow were "Business." The policy prohibited mixing connectors across these groups.

**Resolution:** This is a tenant governance issue, not a configuration error. The fix requires a Power Platform admin to reclassify the relevant Copilot Studio connector as "Business" in the Default DLP policy. Switching from SharePoint to OneDrive does not resolve it — the conflict is with the Copilot Studio knowledge source connector itself, which covers both.

**Key detail for the admin:** The policy change is made in the Power Platform Admin Center under Policies → Data Policies. The connector to reclassify is "Knowledge source with SharePoint and OneDrive in Copilot Studio."

