## 10. Tool Description Is the Single Most Important Configuration

**The finding:** The wording of a tool's description in the Copilot Studio Tools tab directly determines whether the orchestrator calls the tool automatically, when it calls it, and what it passes.

**What a bad description causes:** The orchestrator treats the tool as a general capability and either ignores it, calls it at the wrong time, or asks the user to provide the input the agent should be passing automatically.

**What a good description causes:** The orchestrator calls the tool at the right step, passes the correct variables, and does not prompt the user.

**Pattern:**
```
Call this tool [immediately after / when condition]. 
Pass [VariableName] as [plain description of what it contains]. 
Do not ask the user for any input. 
Returns [what comes back].
```

This pattern is the difference between a working agent and one that silently fails at the tool-call step.
